.TH EUCLID-CLI-ESM-LIST-OBJECT-ATTRIBUTES 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-esm-list-object-attributes \- list the attributes of a storage object
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli esm list-object-attributes
.BR \-\-ern | \-e
.I ERN
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists every user-defined attribute of a storage object, each with its
value and the type that value is stored as. An object with no
attributes lists an empty set rather than failing.
.PP
Attributes set by an FTP or SFTP transfer server record where an
uploaded object came from:
.I transferServer
names the transfer server that took the upload and
.I transferUser
the user that was logged in to it. See
.BR euclid-cli-ets (1).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-ern " " \fIERN\fR
Euclid resource name of the object. Required.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The attributes are printed as JSON: the object's ERN, the attributes
by name, and their count.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the server could not be reached, no object
with that ERN exists, or the object belongs to another account.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 esm list-object-attributes \e
    --ern ern:esm:eu-central-1:000000000000:development:object:mix/PIM-4269.xml
.fi
.RE
.PP
Output:
.RS
.nf
{
  "ern": "ern:esm:eu-central-1:000000000000:development:object:mix/PIM-4269.xml",
  "attributes": {
    "revision": { "type": "long", "value": 7 },
    "transferServer": { "type": "string", "value": "ftp-server" },
    "transferUser": { "type": "string", "value": "admin" }
  },
  "total": 3
}
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-esm (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-add-object-attribute (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-set-object-attribute (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-delete-object-attribute (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-list-objects (1)
